			"notes": "Caustica 0.1.1 improves performance, stability, compatibility, and rendering\nquality across the ray-traced world.\n\n- Smoother terrain and entity rendering with lower CPU and GPU memory usage.\n- Added connected-texture support for Continuity resource packs.\n- Improved rendering for water, banners, paintings, fishing lines, leads,\n  entities, and block entities.\n- Fixed HDR output on Linux systems using native Wayland.\n- Improved Vulkan compatibility and stability across a wider range of systems.\n- Corrected texture colors and completed translations for the emission debug\n  views.\n\nCaustica is still experimental. If you encounter a visual issue or crash,\nplease report it with your latest log."
		},
